{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2184-04-13 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. I’ll be helping manage your care today. How are you feeling right now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2184-04-13 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, doctor. Honestly, I’m in a lot of pain—more than usual. It’s that same crampy, colicky feeling, but worse on the right side. I threw up about two liters of greenish fluid last night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2184-04-13 11:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you mentioned this has been going on for a while, but this episode was worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2184-04-13 11:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. I usually vomit a few times a day, but not this much. And my G-tube isn’t helping like it used to. They switched me to a smaller, more flexible one, and it just doesn’t drain well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2184-04-13 11:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’ve reviewed your CT scan from this morning. It shows that the loops of your small bowel are more dilated than before—about 5 to 6 centimeters—which suggests your chronic partial bowel obstruction may be a bit worse right now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2184-04-13 11:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. So it’s not a new blockage, just the old one acting up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2184-04-13 11:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. It’s the same area, likely in the left lower quadrant, just a little more distended. Surgery was consulted, and they agree no operation is needed at this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2184-04-13 11:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve had enough surgeries. What’s the plan then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2184-04-13 11:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you NPO—nothing by mouth—for now to let your bowel rest. You’ll get IV fluids, and we’ll restart your TPN through your femoral line once we’re sure things are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2184-04-13 11:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And for pain? I know my usual ER protocol is up to 1 mg of IV Dilaudid over an hour."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2184-04-13 11:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s still the plan. We’ll start with 0.25 mg every 15 minutes as needed, up to 1 mg total. We’ll also give you Phenergan for nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2184-04-13 11:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I usually don’t take narcotics at home, so I don’t want to get used to them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2184-04-13 11:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. This is just for acute flare-ups like today. We’ll use it short-term and then stop once you’re back to baseline."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2184-04-13 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. You’ve had a dose of Dilaudid and Phenergan. How’s the pain now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2184-04-13 14:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. Still there, but not as sharp. The nausea’s calmed down too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2184-04-13 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Your labs came back—white count is normal, no signs of infection. Your kidney and liver function are stable. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2184-04-13 14:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had a headache earlier. I use butorphanol nasal spray at home, but I didn’t bring it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2184-04-13 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We gave you a dose of Fioricet, and the nurse said your headache improved quickly. We can arrange for butorphanol to be sent from home or pharmacy if you’d like."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2184-04-13 14:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’d be great. It works better for me than anything else."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2184-04-13 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve been watching you for a few hours. Your pain is more manageable, and you haven’t vomited since admission. We’re going to try a small sip of water to see how you tolerate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2184-04-13 17:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? I haven’t had anything to drink in hours. I’ll try."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2184-04-13 19:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You kept the water down, so we’re advancing to clear liquids. If you do well, we may try soft food tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2184-04-13 19:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good news. What about my G-tube? I really think it’s not working as well since the change."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2184-04-13 19:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We noted that. The team agrees it may not be decompressing effectively. You’re scheduled to follow up with your GI doctor to discuss switching back to a larger tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2184-04-13 19:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. That’s been bothering me a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You did really well overnight—no vomiting, pain is down, and you tolerated a soft diet. Your repeat labs are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So does that mean I can go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’re going to discharge you today. We’ll restart your TPN at home, and you can resume all your regular medications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No changes to my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "None. Everything stays the same—your gabapentin, clonidine, octreotide, all of it. We’ll send a list with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the Dilaudid protocol for future ER visits?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s still valid. The ER and your pain team know the plan: up to 1 mg IV Dilaudid over an hour, with Phenergan if needed, then discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’d like to avoid being admitted again if possible."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We agree. This stay was just to get you through a flare-up safely. Your condition is stable now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the fatty liver the CT mentioned?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s been seen before and is stable. It’s likely related to your TPN. Your hepatology team monitors that, and no new action is needed now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my iron and thyroid meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue both. Your anemia is chronic, and thyroid levels are stable. Keep taking levothyroxine and ferrous sulfate daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my femoral line? It’s clean, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, site is clean and dry. Keep using the ethanol lock as prescribed after TPN to prevent infections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. A nurse will go over discharge instructions, and you should follow up with your GI doctor about the G-tube. Feel better soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’ll see you only if you really need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s the plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will be in shortly with your discharge paperwork."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well. Just keep monitoring your symptoms and reach out if things worsen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Appreciate all the help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2184-04-14 08:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2184-04-13 11:00:00",
    "admission_end": "2184-04-14 14:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a complex history of sclerosing mesenteritis, chronic partial small bowel obstruction, and gastrostomy dependence was admitted for increased abdominal pain and bilious vomiting. Imaging showed slightly worsened dilation of proximal small bowel loops, consistent with her chronic condition. She was managed conservatively with bowel rest, IV fluids, and her established pain protocol using IV Dilaudid and Phenergan. Surgery recommended no intervention. She tolerated a trial of oral intake, her symptoms improved, and she was discharged home in stable condition. All home medications were continued without changes, and she was advised to follow up regarding her G-tube size. TPN was resumed at discharge.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified intestinal obstruction"
    ]
  }
}
